    SL=58, D_self=46, SL-2*D_self=-34
    SL + excess - D = 58 + 66 - 122 = 2 (should be 0 if E=(T-D)/2 worked)


========================================================================
  THE CORRECTED FORMULA
========================================================================


  THE FORMULA E = (T - D) / 2 IS WRONG.

  It fails at n=6 (and actually at n=3 too, masked by integer division).

  The correct decomposition:
  T = SL + 2*E + excess_cross
  where:
    SL = sum_C mult(C -> C) = self-loop orbits
    excess_cross = sum_{{C,D}} (mult(C->D) + mult(D->C) - 2) for C≠D connected
                 = cross_total - 2*E

  So: E = (T - SL - excess_cross) / 2

  Both SL and excess_cross require computing orbit targets, not just counts.
  There is no closed-form expression for E from T and D alone.


========================================================================
  CAN WE COMPUTE SL FROM BURNSIDE?
========================================================================

  n=3: 1/2 classes have |Aut| > 1
  n=4: 2/4 classes have |Aut| > 1
  n=5: 5/12 classes have |Aut| > 1
  n=6: 15/56 classes have |Aut| > 1

========================================================================
  THE EDGE FORMULA: WHAT WE CAN COMPUTE
========================================================================

  n=3: T-2E = 2 = SL(2) + excess(0), (T-2E)/T = 0.5000
  n=4: T-2E = 6 = SL(6) + excess(0), (T-2E)/T = 0.3750
  n=5: T-2E = 28 = SL(16) + excess(12), (T-2E)/T = 0.3182
  n=6: T-2E = 124 = SL(58) + excess(66), (T-2E)/T = 0.1761

  At higher n (from known T and E):
  n=3: T-2E = 2, (T-2E)/T = 0.500000
  n=4: T-2E = 6, (T-2E)/T = 0.375000
  n=5: T-2E = 28, (T-2E)/T = 0.318182
  n=6: T-2E = 124, (T-2E)/T = 0.176136
  n=7: T-2E = 740, (T-2E)/T = 0.083034
  n=8: T-2E = 5966, (T-2E)/T = 0.031686
  n=9: T-2E = 85698, (T-2E)/T = 0.012516

  T-2E = SL + excess_cross. This sum DECREASES relative to T.
  So E ~ T/2 becomes exact at large n.

